(text "J12 and J10 (GPIO_1) are passed through pin for pin. Net names are the base board names. J10 pins 11/29 are named J10_VIN/J10_3V3: same supply as VIN/3V3, tied on both QMTECH boards, not linked on the backplane. (QMTECH schematic 2024-06-07, page 5).\nJ12 pins 12 and 30 are GND, pin 32 is LED5 (the A4 table was wrong)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 20.32 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left top)) (uuid "9de72fdb-629e-51ea-9b4a-ad9492c205e1"))
(text "USB: Cyclone JP6 (USB3300 host) -> Adafruit 5997 USBHOST. JP6 shares D+/D- with the Cyclone J13 USB-A: leave J13 empty.\nHub power = JP6 pin 2 (USB_5V, current limited by the Cyclone U13 TPS2553/TPS25221). It also feeds the I/O USB 5V,\nthe AUX and DISPLAY headers and the Wi-Fi USB-A. On the module all 5V pads and all GND pads are one net.\nHub ports: P1 = I/O Board, P2 = DISPLAY, P3 = Wi-Fi USB-A, P4 = AUX (P3/P4 swapped against the brief to avoid vias)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 167.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left top)) (uuid "17a28071-2100-5358-a15e-d256572cdb9c"))
(text "J6 is PROVISIONAL: it assumes the I/O Board V2.1 has a 2x2 socket over the base JP6.\nCheck on the real board before ordering." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 246.38 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6)) (justify left top)) (uuid "9c0f902f-20cb-5b93-83c6-7a92ab3084b0"))
